			<div class="content" id="post-content-3816018">
									

<p>I'm going to novote because it certainly isn't bad enough to warrant a downvote, but I feel like there needs to be something.. more?</p>
<p>The clinical tone, grammar, and usage of vocabulary throughout this article is absolutely superb. I just have a few problems with the note at the end and a bit about the concept overall.</p>
<p>With the note, I wouldn't call the Serpent's Hand an organization, it's more of a movement; an ideology. So, yes, a select few could be the ones going after him and not staying true to the cause of the SH, but I wouldn't blane the entirety of the wanderers.</p>
<p>With the concept, it just kinda&#8230; appeared? And all it does is make stuff not work? In the containment procedures, why not just restrict usage instead of using amnestics? Wouldn't testing just to forget what you did be a bit unnecessary?</p>
<p>I feel like there should be more about this book. It piqued my interest at the beginning of the description, but I just feel like this article as a whole isn't fleshed out enough.</p>
<p>Best of luck!</p>

